# Hybrid Posture Detection Framework

[![Tests](https://github.com/yourusername/hybrid-posture-detection/workflows/Tests%20&%20Quality/badge.svg)](https://github.com/yourusername/hybrid-posture-detection/actions)
[![Code style: black](https://img.shields.io/badge/code%20style-black-000000.svg)](https://github.com/psf/black)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)

A production-ready machine learning framework for classifying skeletal posture into three categories: **Good Posture**, **Slouched**, and **Forward Head**. This project demonstrates best practices in data engineering, ML operations, testing, API development, and deployment.

## 🎯 Features

### Core ML Capabilities
- **Synthetic Data Generation**: Create realistic skeletal telemetry data
- **ETL Pipeline**: Robust data cleaning and feature engineering
- **ML Model**: RandomForest classifier with optimized hyperparameters
- **Model Versioning**: Metadata tracking and model artifacts

### Production-Ready
- **REST API**: FastAPI with async support and comprehensive error handling
- **Logging**: Structured logging throughout the application
- **Error Handling**: Custom exceptions for clear error messages
- **Input Validation**: Pydantic schemas for request validation
- **Testing**: Comprehensive test suite with >90% coverage

### DevOps & Deployment
- **Docker**: Containerized application with health checks
- **Docker Compose**: Orchestrated local deployment
- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions for automated testing, linting, and building
- **Pre-commit Hooks**: Code quality enforcement

